  "limitations": [
    "V2 is a transport repair after v1's documented PublicNode historical-state HTTP 403; v1 is immutable and is not rerun.",
    "PublicNode documents archive data behind a separate Get Archive Access entry, so v2 uses its public endpoint only for chain identity and historical block headers.",
    "Blockscout is the only historical state provider in v2. Two-provider header identity anchors the block, but configuration and aggregate values are not independently state-replicated or verified with Ethereum state proofs.",
    "Source metadata, deployed-bytecode hashes and the D0b parent triangulate implementation semantics, but Blockscout source REST and state RPC are not independent organizations.",
    "Exact T-minus-one saturation proves that any positive collateral supply would have exceeded the old cap at that state; it does not identify who attempted or intended to supply.",
    "A slack cap can still constrain deposits larger than the remaining headroom, but the counterfactual depositor and order-size distribution are not observed in this zero-account audit.",
    "Fixed block-offset snapshots are diagnostics and do not prove continuous saturation between observations.",
    "No post-event aggregate total is queried, because end-of-block state can mix the governance mechanism with same-block participant response.",
    "Even a pass authorizes only a separately frozen market-level collateral-flow design; account, action, price and response rows remain locked.",
    "The four mechanics survivors are all cap increases in two markets during 2022-2023, including two events for the same WETH-market asset; this is not independent cross-market replication."
  ],
